Load decks of bsim3 against ngspice-45, written by ../load.py bsim3 (R96: the corpus cards, both oracles).
Builds on PATH: ngspice-45 jfngv2gd3zvi5cmr9vrqfhnziipqd09n (level 8 BSIM3v3.3, level 14 BSIM4v8), VACASK
dhxz6l3iac3r2b8n91kcz04a0j3hs4s6 (spice/bsim3v3.osdi, sp_bsim3v3). Card: cards/bsim3.params: ngspice-45 examples/mos/modelcard.nmos (level 8, version 3.3.0). Instance: w=10u l=0.35u, regions (vgs, vds) cut (0.3, 2), lin (3, 0.2), sat (1.5, 3), bulk -0.5 V.
Run: `nix develop .#testing -c tests/fixtures/families/load_run.sh bsim3` (checked). i(vd) in A, |i(vd)| at 1 GHz for acg/acd.
Conditions: nom (27 C, m=1), m3 (27 C, m=3, the multiplier's control), off (80 C, m=3).
Oracles (fd.py): each nominal region's gm and gds by central differences of each simulator's own DC against its 1 kHz AC
reading; every m3 reading 3 times its nom (no failing row printed).
Result: no difference. The two simulators agree to 4e-12 on every DC and AC reading; VACASK's AC is its DC slope to 4e-10,
ngspice's to its 12 printed digits (1e-6 at most where the slope is small); the m relation holds on both. The transient
with the charges (../tran/ and ../tran_fine/, bsim3) agrees to step control (shrinking with the step).

